 November 08, 2026 at 3:00 PM to consider, among others, Un-Audited Financial Statements for the First Quarter (Q1) period ended September 30, 2026."},{"day":"2026-10-26","title":"Trading of the shares of the company will resume on 27-Oct-2026.","body":"Trading of the shares of the company will resume on 27-Oct-2026."},{"day":"2026-10-25","title":"Trading of the shares of the company will remain suspended on record date i.e., ","body":"Trading of the shares of the company will remain suspended on record date i.e., 26.10.2026."},{"day":"2026-10-18","title":"Trading of the shares of the company will be allowed only in the Spot Market and","body":"Trading of the shares of the company will be allowed only in the Spot Market and Block transaction will also be settled as per spot settlement cycle with cum benefit from 19.10.2026 to 25.10.2026 and trading of the shares will remain suspended on record date i.e., 26.10.2026."},{"day":"2026-09-28","title":"There will be no price limit on the trading of the shares of the Company today (","body":"There will be no price limit on the trading of the shares of the Company today (28.09.2026) following its corporate declaration."},{"day":"2026-09-28","title":"The Board of Directors has recommended 32.50\\% Cash Dividend for the year ended ","body":"The Board of Directors has recommended 32.50\\% Cash Dividend for the year ended June 30, 2026. Date of AGM: 05 December 2026 at 11:00 AM, Venue: Hybrid System at Gulshan Shooting Club, Gulshan Avenue, beside Police Plaza, Dhaka-1212. Record Date: 26 October 2026. The Company has also reported EPS of Tk. 8.24, NAV per share of Tk. 60.33 and NOCFPS of Tk. 14.88 for the year ended June 30, 2026 as against Tk. 8.40, Tk. 58.32 and Tk. 4.77 respectively for the year ended June 30, 2025."},{"day":"2026-09-20","title":"As per Regulation 19(1) of the Dhaka Stock Exchange (Listing) Regulations, 2015,","body":"As per Regulation 19(1) of the Dhaka Stock Exchange (Listing) Regulations, 2015, the Company has informed that a meeting of the Board of Directors will be held on September 27, 2026 at 3:00 PM to consider, among others, audited financial statements of the Company for the year ended June 30, 2026."},{"day":"2026-07-15","title":"(Cont. News of ENVOYTEX)","body":"(Cont. News of ENVOYTEX): This has enabled the Company to overcome the previous bottleneck in the upstream process and now fully utilize its existing back-process capacity, resulting in improved overall operational efficiency and output. (end)"},{"day":"2026-07-15","title":"The company has informed that the Board of Directors in its meeting held on 14 J","body":"The company has informed that the Board of Directors in its meeting held on 14 July 2026 has taken cognizance of the Company\\'s increased annual denim fabrics production capacity from 52 million yards to 60 million yards. The enhanced capacity, which is already in commercial production, has been achieved through upgradation of certain upstream production facilities and introduction of automation. (cont.)"},{"day":"2026-04-27","title":"The company has informed that the Board of Directors in its meeting held on 26 A","body":"The company has informed that the Board of Directors in its meeting held on 26 April 2026, has approved to purchase 50.37 decimal land in the adjacent area of the company\\'s factory at Jamirda, Bhaluka, Mymensingh, Bangladesh at a total approximate cost of Tk. 8.09 crore including Registration and other costs. The said land will be used for the future extension of the factory."},{"day":"2026-04-27","title":"(Cont. news of ENVOYTEX)","body":"(Cont. news of ENVOYTEX): Based on projected operating efficiency and current cost and pricing assumptions, the project is expected to generate sufficient cash flows to service the 7-year term loan. It is expected to achieve a payback period of approximately 4.8 years, with an Equity IRR of 27.8\\% and a Project IRR of 14.8\\% over the 15-year project life. (end)"},{"day":"2026-04-27","title":"(Cont. news of ENVOYTEX)","body":"(Cont. news of ENVOYTEX): and to leverage currently underutilized capacity. The yarn produced will be prioritized for in-house denim manufacturing to maximize vertical integration and operational efficiency. The total estimated cost of the project is BDT 1,791.53 million, to be financed through a debt-equity ratio of 70:30 The expansion project will feature state-of-the-art open-end rotor spinning yarn production facilities. (cont.2)"},{"day":"2026-04-27","title":"The company has informed that the Board of Directors of the company during its 2","body":"The company has informed that the Board of Directors of the company during its 252nd Meeting held on 26 April 2026 has approved the expansion of Open-End (Rotor) Spinning production capacity from the existing 25 MT per day to 50 MT per day at the existing factory premises. The project aims to increase yarn production capacity to utilize recovered materials from existing production processes (cont.1)"},{"day":"2026-04-27","title":"(Q3 Un-audited)","body":"(Q3 Un-audited): EPS was Tk. 1.54 for January-March 2026 as against Tk. 2.44 for January-March 2025; EPS was Tk. 5.89 for July 2025-March 2026 as against Tk. 6.03 for July 2024-March 2025. NOCFPS was Tk. 16.85 for July 2025-March 2026 as against Tk. 3.27 for July 2024-March 2025. NAV per share was Tk. 61.21 as on March 31, 2026 and Tk. 58.32 as on June 30, 2025."}],"sources":[{"name":"stocknow","ok":true,"url":"https://stocknow.com.bd/stocks/ENVOYTEX","error":null},{"name":"amarstock","ok":true,"url":"https://www.amarstock.com/stock/ENVOYTEX","error":null},{"name":"topstock","ok":true,"url":"https://www.topstockbd.com/stock/ENVOYTEX","error":null}],"units":{"capital":"BDT million (total_shares is a count)","financial_years":"BDT; eps, nav_per_share, nocfps are Tk per share","statements":"BDT as reported; per-share rows in Tk","dividends":"% of the Tk 10 face value; cash_per_share in Tk"},"price":85.6,"ratios":[{"key":"roe",